From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nouveau/gm20b: Add an option to disable the NA PLL

On a Jetson Nano (speedo 2), the first GR init after boot fails much more
often with the noise-aware GPC PLL than with the non-NA path used on
speedo 0 parts: with devfreq polling disabled, 5 of 20 boots against 0 of
10. Failing boots time out in the PMU, or, when checked, show SEL_VCO
refusing to leave bypass although the PLL reports lock.

Add NvNaPll=0 to select the speedo 0 clock and voltage handling on any
GM20B. The two go together: the NA voltage table is lower and relies on
the PLL to follow voltage droop.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/clk/gm20b.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/clk/gm20b.c
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <subdev/volt.h>
 #include <subdev/timer.h>
 #include <core/device.h>
+#include <core/option.h>
 #include <core/tegra.h>
 
 #include "priv.h"
@@ -1025,8 +1026,12 @@
 	struct gk20a_clk_pllg_params *clk_params;
 	int ret;
 
-	/* Speedo 0 GPUs cannot use noise-aware PLL */
-	if (tdev->gpu_speedo_id == 0)
+	/*
+	 * Speedo 0 GPUs cannot use noise-aware PLL. On others it can be turned
+	 * off with NvNaPll=0, which must match the voltage table volt uses.
+	 */
+	if (tdev->gpu_speedo_id == 0 ||
+	    !nvkm_boolopt(device->cfgopt, "NvNaPll", true))
 		return gm20b_clk_new_speedo0(device, type, inst, pclk);
 
 	/* Speedo >= 1, use NAPLL */
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/volt/gm20b.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/volt/gm20b.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include "priv.h"
 #include "gk20a.h"
 
+#include <core/option.h>
 #include <core/tegra.h>
 
 static const struct cvb_coef gm20b_cvb_coef[] = {
@@ -84,7 +85,9 @@
 
 	vmin = speedo_to_vmin[tdev->gpu_speedo_id];
 
-	if (tdev->gpu_speedo_id >= 1)
+	/* The NA table assumes the clock uses the noise-aware PLL */
+	if (tdev->gpu_speedo_id >= 1 &&
+	    nvkm_boolopt(device->cfgopt, "NvNaPll", true))
 		return gk20a_volt_ctor(device, type, inst, gm20b_na_cvb_coef,
 				       ARRAY_SIZE(gm20b_na_cvb_coef), vmin, volt);
 	else
